{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"accepted-androgenic-elk","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe Engine B metric backend parses per-file entries from scc JSON, but `_metric_invoke` invokes `scc --format json <repo>` without `--by-file`. With maintained scc 3.7.0, the language summary includes `Files: []` unless `--by-file` is requested. Therefore a present scc process can run successfully while `rebar.builtin.smell.metric-oversize` sees no files and can never emit its documented over-800-LOC matches.\n\nThe analogous code-health adapter defect was fixed by closed bug rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab, whose history explicitly notes grounding `_scc_files` is a separate consumer. Current coverage-reconstruction tests use a 50-LOC fixture or force tool absence, so they do not exercise the positive metric threshold path.\n\n## Reproduction\n- Run `scc --format json tests/unit/grounding` and inspect each language `Files` array: it is empty.\n- Compare with `scc --by-file --format json tests/unit/grounding`: per-file entries are present.\n- Inspect `src/rebar/grounding/engine_b_backends.py::_metric_invoke`: its command omits `--by-file` while `_scc_files` depends on `Files`.\n\n## Plan\n- Use rebar-debug to reproduce with a real scc binary and an over-800-code-line fixture, then prove the exact argv cause before editing.\n- Add a physically withheld RED oracle that observes a real or argv-faithful scc boundary and fails when `--by-file` is absent.\n- Correct the grounding metric invocation without changing thresholds or fail-open semantics.\n- Add positive match, below-threshold no-match, invalid-output, nonzero-exit, and tool-absent coverage.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A present scc run over a file above the configured LOC threshold emits a normalized metric match for that file.\n- [ ] A present scc run below the threshold emits no fabricated match.\n- [ ] The scc command requests per-file JSON explicitly; checked by an argv-sensitive test.\n- [ ] Tool absence, timeout/nonzero failure, and invalid JSON remain fail-open evidence outcomes.\n- [ ] The focused grounding backend tests pass with the held-out exact-defect oracle.\n\n## Verification\n- Run the focused grounding metric tests with the worktree virtualenv.\n- Run the repository lint and typecheck gates.\n- Run the default test suite before landing through Gerrit.","id":"0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["grounding","bug","scc"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Grounding metric detector omits scc --by-file and can never emit file matches"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786910974260071001,"uuid":"98373b2c-e7d9-4304-ad03-e442975c73ac"}